# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — ProcessQueue lifecycle parity
# Recorded: 2026-10-23 00:05:20 UTC
# Code revision: 2ce652e7

## Compatibility finding

Pinned Java 5.5.1 changes `ProcessQueue.consuming` in `putMessage` when it
starts a dispatch and clears the flag only when `takeMessages` returns an
empty list. Nonempty takes, `commit`, `rollback`, and
`makeMessageToConsumeAgain` leave the flag unchanged. `commit` also leaves
`lastConsumeTimestamp` unchanged. Rust's public methods now preserve those
state transitions.

The invoked `ConsumerFacadeApiFixtures` comparison records dispatch after
commit, rollback, and requeue, including a nonempty take while `consuming` is
false, and checks that `commit` preserves the caller-set timestamp. Fixture
SHA-256:
`2e43cc737fa784cdaec0488252000e82360ccd0a4b121e6ee28d2dccf704791e`.

